  "problem": "Suppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Let the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y$ be $F(x,y),$ where\n\n$$\nF(12,6)=0.81,\\,F(12,4)=0.3,\\,F(6,6)=0.17,\\,F(6,4)=0.1,\n$$\n\nand the supports of $X$ and $Y$, respectively, are\n\n$$\n{S}_{X}=\\{3,6,9,12,15\\},\\,{S}_{Y}=\\{2,4,6,8,10\\}.\n$$\n\nFind $P(6<X\\le 12,4<Y\\le 6).$",
